  "id": "DrugBank_DB13092 - MONDO_1246",
  "verbalization": "Meclocycline is implicated in the treatment of Typhus through a chain of indications that connect it to Brucellosis and then to Minocycline, which in turn is linked to Typhus. This suggests a potential pathway where Meclocycline may be used in conjunction with other antibiotics to treat Typhus. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Brucellosis in two of the paths, indicating a possible overlap in therapeutic use. The presence of Minocycline as an intermediate in two of the paths further reinforces the idea that Meclocycline may be part of a broader treatment strategy for Typhus. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Meclocycline to be repurposed in the context of Typhus, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
